{"name":"Maiden Hair","hex":"#f5e9ca","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maiden-hair","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of maidenhair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden-hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adiantum","blocks":[{"text":"Adiantum, the maidenhair fern, is a genus of about 250 species of ferns in the subfamily Vittarioideae of the family Pteridaceae, though some researchers place it in its own family, Adiantaceae. The genus name comes from Greek, meaning \"unwetted\", referring to the fronds' ability to shed water without becoming wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG/330px-Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adiantum"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG/500px-Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG/1280px-Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w